# Bumped 2026-06-25 (overlay cache unification + ws_cull DLL fix): psxrecomp
#   master e7f7fb6 = 1915b5c + the two framework fixes that cured the overlay
#   "agonizing lag" (e.g. Tomba's dwarf village ran ~97% interpreted): (1) the
#   runtime now injects PSX_OVERLAY_CACHE_DIR/PSX_OVERLAY_CAPTURES so the
#   autocompile WRITE cache + READ captures are always the loader's canonical
#   <exe>/cache (no more write-where-the-loader-can't-read drift); (2) the overlay
#   DLL preamble now defines psx_ws_cull_sltiu (auto_screen_x emits it into every
#   build's overlay C; its absence made any overlay variant with cull sites fail to
#   link -> no shard -> interpreter forever). Proven: dwarf village 29/s -> 11454/s
#   native. Runtime/tooling only; codegen unchanged (cache stays cg4_7db781d9).
# Bumped 2026-06-25 (sljit->tcc tier refactor): psxrecomp master 1915b5c =
#   5007c46 + the overlay-backend refactor that RETIRES the buggy sljit emitter
#   tier and replaces it with a TCC (TinyCC) toolchain-free tier. Priority is now
#   static > gcc shard > tcc shard > interp (tcc fills the regions the bundled
#   gcc cache doesn't cover, where uncovered code previously fell to slow interp
#   ??? the source of the user-reported lag). Also folds in the post-BIOS boot
#   snapshot (340d6e7) + "Skip PSX BIOS" launcher toggle (c35c04f) and the SDL
