# so later launches reuse JIT'd shards instead of re-discovering through interp
# (priority gcc > sljit > interp unchanged). VALIDATED: settings persist across
# launches (user-confirmed); two-launch reload test loaded 12 shards at a fresh
# ASLR base with no stale-pointer crash, gameplay rendered. NOTE: the settings
# persistence emits a recompiler init-store hook -> a REGEN is required (game.toml
# + game_options.toml already carry the sites). Supersedes 1b49814.
# ---- prior pin (crash report names the recursion culprit) ----
# Bumped 2026-06-16 (crash report names the recursion culprit): psxrecomp master
# 1b49814. The runaway-recursion crash report now carries an always-on ring of
# the last 64 recompiled function entries (GUEST addresses) + recursion_func (the
# func entered at the guard trip), so the next ORGANIC seesaw/wild-call crash
# names the recursing function build-independently (root-cause in Ghidra, no
# symbol map needed; pair with cpu.gpr for the corrupt args). Validated via the
# synth_recurse debug self-test; no measurable overhead (16:9 stays 60fps), no
# false-trips. Runtime-only. Supersedes 2cf9f4a.
# ---- prior pin (native stack-overflow guard) ----
# Bumped 2026-06-16 (native stack-overflow guard): psxrecomp master 2cf9f4a adds
# a tentative containment for the intermittent watchtower force-close (host stack
# overflow from runaway guest recursion ??? the seesaw/Bug-D wild-call family). An
# in-range guest jal compiles to a direct func_X(cpu) call, so the recursion grew
# the native stack without going through psx_dispatch_impl: the existing depth
# guard was blind (crash report showed dispatch_depth=0). New guard at every
# recompiled function entry reads the fiber's TEB stack bounds and halts
# gracefully (captured crash report; clean exit in release) BEFORE overflow.
# Converts a silent force-close into a parseable report so the crash can be
# root-caused from a repro. Verified no false-trigger; NOT a root fix (upstream
# data corruption unaddressed). Runtime-only. Supersedes f046d52 (still includes
# the GL draw batching 16:9 lag fix below).
# ---- prior pin (GL draw batching ??? 16:9 lag fix) ----
# Bumped 2026-06-16 (GL draw batching ??? 16:9 lag fix): psxrecomp master f046d52
# merges perf/gl-frame-timing. The OpenGL renderer was immediate-mode (~1000
# prims/frame, each its own glDrawArrays at ~14us GPU time ??? pipeline-flush
# overhead; native-wide doubled it). Fixed by batching consecutive textured
# prims sharing blend/mask/texwindow/filter into one draw (per-prim texture
# state moved to flat vertex attributes). Measured (frame_perf, the new GPU/CPU
# phase-timing tooling also in this bump): Tomba village 16:9 scene_gpu
# 28.3->16.0ms (~34->~60fps), 4:3 16.5->5.5ms (3x headroom). Runtime-only
